# Kartograf settings (Nogat DEV-18). Kartograf does not read a .env file: export the
# variables you need in your shell, service or container definition, or put the keys
# in nogat.toml.
#
# A setting comes from the first of: the command-line option, the variable
# KARTOGRAF_<KEY>, NOGAT_<KEY> (only data_dir, cache_dir and lang), the table
# [kartograf] and then [nogat] of nogat.toml (key = the variable without the prefix,
# lower case; [nogat] holds the shared keys only), the default. An empty variable
# counts as unset.
# nogat.toml lives in the user configuration directory (for example
# ~/.config/nogat/nogat.toml) or at the path in NOGAT_CONFIG. Credentials
# (CLMS_CREDENTIALS) are read from the environment only, never from nogat.toml.
# `kartograf config show [--json]` lists every value and where it comes from.

# --- Shared with the other tools (also NOGAT_DATA_DIR, NOGAT_CACHE_DIR, NOGAT_LANG)
# Parent of the stores (<data_dir>/kartograf). Default: the user data directory of
# nogat (for example ~/.local/share/nogat).
# KARTOGRAF_DATA_DIR=
# Parent of the caches: the metadata cache is <cache_dir>/kartograf/metadata.db.
# Default: the user cache directory of nogat (for example ~/.cache/nogat). Use a
# local disk: SQLite is unreliable on network shares.
# KARTOGRAF_CACHE_DIR=
# Language of human-readable output: pl or en. Default: pl.
# KARTOGRAF_LANG=pl

# --- Kartograf only (not a shared key: NOGAT_ROOT and [nogat] root do not exist)
# Root of the store. Default: <data_dir>/kartograf. The commands still take the store
# from --output; this is the root `config show` reports (Nogat DEV-19.2).
# KARTOGRAF_ROOT=
# Print the traceback of an unexpected error and let every library log record
# through in the --json mode: 1 or 0. Default: 0.
# KARTOGRAF_DEBUG=0

# --- Only the shared file
# Path of nogat.toml instead of the one in the user configuration directory.
# NOGAT_CONFIG=

# --- Credential (environment only; never printed, `config show` says present or missing)
# JSON of the Copernicus CLMS API credentials for CORINE as GeoTIFF (docs/USAGE.md 6).
# CLMS_CREDENTIALS=
